# Docker build-context excludes — keep the context lean for fast rebuilds.
# The Dockerfile (deploy/docker/Dockerfile) only needs pyproject.toml, uv.lock,
# src/, and deploy/docker/. Everything below is either huge, host-only, or
# regenerated inside the image, so it must never enter the build context.
# (Do NOT add README.md / pyproject-referenced metadata files here — the wheel
#  build reads them.)

# Version control / local virtualenv (the two biggest offenders)
.git
.gitignore
.venv
venv/
env/

# Private design corpus — never shipped in the image.
#
# ⚠ Docker does not read .git/info/exclude, which is the ONLY firewall separating
# this dual-git working tree's public and private halves (.gitignore deliberately
# does not list the private material — see its header). So every private path must
# be named here explicitly, exactly as it must be named in
# [tool.hatch.build.targets.sdist].exclude for the same reason (ADR-0259).
#
# This is defense in depth, not a live leak: the Dockerfile uses targeted COPY
# lines and has no `COPY . .`, so nothing private reaches the image. But the
# context is transmitted to the daemon and cached — which leaves this machine the
# moment a remote or shared buildx driver is used — and a single future
# `COPY . .` would publish whatever is in it. Measured on this machine, the
# reported build-context transfer went from 13.48 MB to 168 kB once this list was
# completed. (The private paths total ~88 MB on disk, but much of that is already
# caught by the generic rules above — *.log, __pycache__ — so the two numbers are
# not the same thing and should not be conflated.)
#
# tests/docs/test_private_paths_never_enter_a_build.py derives the required set
# from the two gitdirs and fails if a new private path is missing here.
design/
.claude/
.git-private
.claude-plugin/
.dualgit/
CLAUDE.md
THREAT_MODEL.md
experiments/
monetize/
papers/
priv/
ship/
site-config/
.benchmark-results/
_linkcheck_probe.md
# p2p working artifacts. p2p was RETIRED 2026-08-29 and these files no longer
# exist; the entries are kept as a harmless guard in case anything recreates them.
.p2p.toml
.p2p-undo/
.p2p-history.jsonl
.p2p-manifest.json
p2p-sync-report.html

# Node / dashboard build artifacts (source is compiled during the image build)
**/node_modules
web/dist/
web/.astro/
packages/**/dist/

# Python caches & build artifacts
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
build/
dist/
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*

# Local scratch / benches / logs
bench/
*.log

# Compiled Python from the host — never belongs in the image build context.
**/__pycache__/
